## Working agreement
- **Communicate with the user in their language** (mirror the language they write in).
- **Language boundary — split by who reads it, NOT by folder:**
  - **User's language (human-read & maintained):** PRD, design, review, run reports,
    `docs/agent-orchestra/INDEX.md`, **`.claude/agent-memory/`** (the agents' running log — you and
    teammates audit it), and `.claude/knowledge/`. These sit under `.claude/` but people read them,
    so they are written in the user's language — **not** English.
  - **English (portable tool / model-facing config):** the plugin itself, and the generated
    instruction files — `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/agents/*.md`, `.claude/rules/*.md`. (Keeps them
    portable and keeps the agents' verbatim protocol blocks consistent.)
  - So "files under `.claude/` are English" is **wrong** as a blanket rule — agent-memory and
    knowledge are the human-read exceptions and must be in the user's language.
- **Substantive code / design / analysis work → use `/agent-orchestra:run`** — it runs the work as
  an observable Agent Team with an independent reviewer + adversarial critic gate (bias correction).
  Quick questions and one-line edits: just answer/do them directly (plain Claude — Orchestra is not always-on).
- **Do it right the first time:** no temporary measures, no swallowed errors, no silent
  omissions, no "fix later". The critic blocks these.

